  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "Let PPP, QQQ, and RRR be binary strings of equal length LLL.\n\n**Define** F(P,Q,R)F(P,Q,R)F(P,Q,R) as the minimum total cost to transform QQQ into RRR using the\nfollowing rules:\n\n\n\nYou may flip PiP_iPi​ or QiQ_iQi​ for any index iii (1≤i≤L)(1 \\le i \\le L)(1≤i≤L).\nEach flip changes 0↔10 \\leftrightarrow 10↔1 and costs 111.\n\n\n\n\nAfter all flips are completed, you may perform any number of **valid swaps** in the\nresulting string QQQ at zero cost.\n\n\n\n\nA swap of indices iii and jjj in QQQ is **valid swap** if and only if the final values\nof PiP_iPi​ and PjP_jPj​ are equal.\n\n\n\nIt can be proved that it is always possible to transform QQQ into RRR using the above rules.\n\nYou are given three binary strings AAA, BBB, and CCC of length NNN.\n\nCompute F(A,B,C)F(A,B,C)F(A,B,C).\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains two space-separated integers NNN — the length of the strings.\nThe next three lines contain three strings A,BA, BA,B and CCC respectively.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the required value.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\leq T \\leq 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "AAA, BBB, CCC are binary strings",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "6\n1\n0\n0\n0\n3\n010\n010\n010\n4\n1100\n1010\n1001\n5\n00000\n11111\n01010\n6\n101010\n010101\n111000\n8\n00110101\n00100111\n11110000",
        "output": "0\n0\n0\n3\n2\n1",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nFor the first test case, BBB is already equal to CCC, so we do nothing. The cost is 000.\n\n\nFor the second test case, BBB is already equal to CCC, so we do nothing. The cost is 000.\n\n\nFor the third test case, one optimal way is:\n\nPerform no flips.\nDo a valid swap in BBB: swap indices 333 and 444.\nThis swap is valid because A3=0A_3 = 0A3​=0 and A4=0A_4 = 0A4​=0, so the values of AAA at these indices are equal, and the swap costs 000.\nAfter this swap, BBB becomes exactly CCC, so no flips are needed.\nTotal cost = 000.\n\n\n\nFor the fourth test case, one optimal way is:\n\nFlip B1B_1B1​ from 1 to 0, cost 111.\nFlip B3B_3B3​ from 1 to 0, cost 111.\nFlip B4B_4B4​ from 1 to 0, cost 111.\nSwap B4B_4B4​ and B5B_5B5​.\nNow BBB becomes equal to CCC.\nTotal cost = 333."
      }
    ]
  },
